The function `unobstructed_buildings` will iterate through the list of building heights from right to left, tracking the maximum height encountered. For each building, if its height is greater than the current maximum, it is added to the result list. The indices are then sorted and returned.

```python
def unobstructed_buildings(heights: List[int]) -> List[int]:
    unobstructed_indices = []
    max_height = -1
    for i in range(len(heights) - 1, -1, -1):
        if heights[i] > max_height:
            unobstructed_indices.append(i)
            max_height = heights[i]
    return sorted(unobstructed_indices)
